## Context
After ticket 0116, the `Erg` struct carries diagnostic-trace fields
(`Unknown`, `RepeatedSingletons`, `ClosedEmpty`, `ClosedInLog`,
`ClosedInBody`, `HasLogSep`, `HasBodySep`) that exist only so the
separate validator can re-derive what the parser already saw. This is
two passes over the same information.

A validating parser emits parse errors directly as it walks the file.
The trace fields collapse to zero. `parseErg` becomes the single source
of truth for both shape and error reporting.

## Proposed signature change
```go
// Before
func parseErg(path string) Erg
func validateErg(t *Erg, allIDs map[string]bool) []string

// After
func parseErg(path string) (Erg, []ParseError)
// Corpus-level checks (Blocked-by resolution, cycle detection) stay
// separate — they need the full corpus, not a single file.
func validateCorpus(tickets []Erg) []ValidationError
```

Per-file rules (1-9, 11-13) move into the parser. Corpus-level rules
(10: Blocked-by ID resolution; cycle detection) stay in a thin corpus
walker that consumes already-parsed `Erg` values.

## Actions
1. Define a `ParseError` type with file, line, rule, message fields.
2. In `parseErg`, emit `ParseError` values as each per-file rule fires
   (today's rules 1-9, 11-13 plus the relaxed rule 12).
3. Delete the trace fields from `Erg` (the user of each disappears with
   the corresponding validator branch).
4. Delete `validateErg` (per-file rules). Rename or refactor the
   corpus-level checks into `validateCorpus`.
5. Update `cmdValidate` and `cmdCheck` to call the new entry points.
6. Update tests: validate_test.go gets restructured around parser
   output; new fixtures for error reporting shape.

## Out of scope
- Type tightening (`BlockedBys []Ref`, `Created time.Time`). Filed
  separately so this ticket stays focused on the pass merge.
- Changes to validator rules themselves; only the architecture moves.

## Dependencies
- Hard dep: ticket 0116 (schema-literal struct). The diagnostic-trace
  fields removed here are the ones 0116 introduces; they must exist
  before they can be eliminated.

## Exit criteria
- `Erg` struct contains no diagnostic-trace fields — only schema and
  body/log content.
- `parseErg` returns `(Erg, []ParseError)`.
- Per-file rules emit errors at parse time, not in a separate pass.
- Corpus-level rules (ref resolution, cycles) live in a clearly-named
  corpus walker.
- `make test` passes; error messages preserved or improved.
